{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-263046-r4515339","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Stroopwafels","sourcePageId":263046,"sourceRevision":"4515339","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T03:08:46Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Stroopwafels&oldid=4515339","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:52.726Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Dessert recipes","Category:Dutch recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for cookies","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using corn syrup","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using hazelnut","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Snack recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"2b2077164c06a744c90f627df338813619e705f02a824b77ce605b8660155964","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Cookie recipes|servings=12|time=About 2 hours|difficulty=3\n| Image = [[File:Gaufre biscuit.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Waffle|Waffle]] | [[Cookbook:Snack|Snack]]\n\n'''Stroopwafels''' are a kind of [[Cookbook:Cookie|cookie]], originating in The Netherlands. They are typically a morning or evening snack eaten with tea or coffee. They are slightly chewy in texture and made with different fillings and flavors. The following recipe has been adapted from the Diana Dessert recipe [http://dianasdesserts.com/index.cfm/fuseaction/recipes.recipeListing/filter/dianas/recipeID/694/Recipe.cfm].\n\n==Ingredients==\n===Waffles===\n*1 package (¼ [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounce]]) active dry [[Cookbook:Yeast|yeast]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] warm water \n*4 cups [[Cookbook:Flour|all-purpose flour]]\n*1 cup unsalted [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:White Sugar|white sugar]]\n*2 large [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n\n===Filling===\n*1½ cups packed [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*1 cup unsalted [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*1 tsp ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n*6 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] dark [[Cookbook:Corn Syrup|corn syrup]]\n*½ cup finely-ground [[Cookbook:Hazelnut|hazelnuts]], optional\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Waffles ===\n#Preheat a Pizzelle iron.\n#Dissolve the yeast in the warm water.\n#Add the butter to the flour, then mix in the sugar, cinnamon, eggs, and yeast mixture.\n#Mix well and set aside to rise for 30–60 minutes.\n#Roll dough into 12 small balls, squeeze each ball into the preheated pizzelle iron, and cook for about 30 seconds.\n\n===Filling===\n#In a [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]], cook the brown sugar, butter, cinnamon, and dark corn syrup until it reaches the [[Cookbook:Cooking Sugar|soft ball stage]] (234–240°F or 112–115°C).\n#Stir in ground hazelnuts at this point, if using.\n\n===Assembly===\n#Cut each waffle into two thin layers and sandwich them with some filling.\n#Repeat this process until all the filling and waffles are used.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* If using hazelnuts, remove skin, if possible. Grind hazelnuts in a [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]] until they are ground to a fine powder.\n* Try eating your stroopwafel by resting it over a warm cup of coffee or tea. The steam will warm these up just right.\n* Collect any remains of the waffles and let them cool. They can be served as \"crumbs\" and are usually also sold as such.\n\n[[Category:Snack recipes]]\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Dutch recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for cookies]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn syrup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using hazelnut]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Stroopwafels","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 package (¼ ounce) active dry yeast","sourceText":"1 package (¼ ounce) active dry yeast","amountText":"1 package (¼ ounce) active dry yeast","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup warm water","sourceText":"½ cup warm water","amountText":"½ cup warm water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"4 cups all-purpose flour","sourceText":"4 cups all-purpose flour","amountText":"4 cups all-purpose flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup unsalted butter","sourceText":"1 cup unsalted butter","amountText":"1 cup unsalted butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ tsp ground cinnamon","sourceText":"½ tsp ground cinnamon","amountText":"½ tsp ground cinnamon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"½ cup white sugar","sourceText":"½ cup white sugar","amountText":"½ cup white sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 large eggs","sourceText":"2 large eggs","amountText":"2 large eggs","amount":null,"u